  "question": {
    "text": "In an examination, $62 \\%$ of the candidates failed in English, 42% in Mathematics and 20% in both. The number of those who passed in both the subjects is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uWXDM",
      "text": "$11$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "O4feV",
      "text": "$16$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zBzfF",
      "text": "$18$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FpA7S",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/9I5DBY6wMJkndyAmE6yLVCTcpiLnHc7dbS0ZZNkrNDw.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nFrom the given condition,\n$\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{c}=62 \\mathrm{k} ; \\mathrm{b}+\\mathrm{c}=42 \\mathrm{k}$ and $\\mathrm{c}=20 \\mathrm{k}$\nHence $\\mathrm{a}=42 \\mathrm{k}$ and $\\mathrm{b}=22 \\mathrm{k}$\nNumber of students who failed in none means passed in both $=\\mathrm{n}=100 \\mathrm{k}-(\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{b}+\\mathrm{c})$\n$=100 \\mathrm{k}-(42 \\mathrm{k}+22 \\mathrm{k}+20 \\mathrm{k})=16 \\mathrm{k}$. or $16 \\%$",
    "image": null
  },
